  "term": "nasal cavity",
  "definition": "The nasal cavity is the inside space of the nose, where both non-tumorous and tumorous growths can occur. In the source material, it is described as a site with varied lesion types, most commonly non-neoplastic masses such as nasal polyps, while benign and malignant tumors are less common.",
